    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36612" root="كت" body-key="k">
    
      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تكاتّو عَلَيْهِ</span></b>  <i>They pressed together,</i> or <i>crowded
together, upon it, with crying,</i> or <i>noise:</i> from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكَتِيتُ</span>. Occurring in a trad., as related and
explained by Z; but the word commonly known
is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تكابّوا</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span>. (TA.)

